  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ethiopia-Netherlands Seed Partnership will enable the private sector in Ethiopia to deliver farming men and women high quality seed of improved va</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AA1 This adjustment concerns a top-up and extension of the Ethiopia-Netherlands Seed Partnership 2021-2025. Supplementary funding of EUR 523.364 until  31-12-2028.
Not part of our commitment is the complementary funding of the EU in the context of the Delegated Cooperation modality. EU will contribute to the program an amount of  EUR 7.476.636 from 1/1/2024. Disbursement from the EU will be made to a special DC account managed by FEZ.  The current amendment (to be signed after in our after April 2024) will start with retrospective effect from 1.1.2024 to align with the EU and avoid double reporting and follows the NL calendar year Jan-Dec. The delay is due to a lengthy process with WUR to come to terms on different subjects due to the new modality. Please note that the formal name of  the program towards the EU is ESP+. Further delays occurred through the approval process of new commitments &gt; EUR 100.000 by DGIS, which was finally approved 21 June 2024, and personal changes.</narrative>
  </description>
